{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966809,"nonce":"iEmkOhNf+MRAiBuWFjwuw++z+2E=","title":"render_tree_with_motion_opt's z-layered no-glass branch built a temporary z0_batch with","message":"On web (any 1×-sample target — webgpu / webgl), node_editor_demo's SVG icons (cylinder for source, funnel for filter, monitor for sink, \"A\" for formatter, golden diamond for subgraph) rendered at degenerate / stale positions while node bodies tracked viewport changes correctly. Specifically:\n\n- Initial paint: icons missing or at wrong positions.\n- Open a context menu / dialog (any overlay that triggers a subtree rebuild): icons rendered correctly for that frame.\n- Zoom or pan: icons stuck at pre-interaction positions while everything else moved.\n\nDesktop was unaffected.\n\n\n`crates/blinc_app/src/context.rs:9818-9822` (no-glass / z-layered branch of `render_tree_with_motion_opt`):\n\n```rust\nlet z0_primitives = batch.primitives_for_layer(0);\nlet mut z0_batch = PrimitiveBatch::new();\nz0_batch.primitives = z0_primitives;\nz0_batch.paths = batch.paths.clone();\nself.renderer.render_with_clear(target, \u0026z0_batch, ...);\n```\n\n`PrimitiveBatch::new()` defaults `aux_data` to `vec![]`. The clone copied `primitives` + `paths` but NOT `aux_data`. `render_with_clear` then uploaded the empty slice to the GPU's `aux_data` storage buffer via `update_aux_data_buffer(z0_batch)` → `queue.write_buffer(aux_data, 0, \u0026[])`.\n\nThe MESH primitive vertex shader (`sdf_core.wgsl:256-266`) reads triangle vertex positions from `aux_data[border.z]`:\n\n```wgsl\nif prim.type_info.x == 9u {\n    let aux_off = u32(prim.border.z);\n    let pack0 = aux_data[aux_off];\n    let pack1 = aux_data[aux_off + 1u];\n    ...\n}\n```\n\nWith the buffer wiped, every MESH primitive — `fill_path` / `stroke_path` with a solid or gradient brush, which goes through `push_mesh_primitives_brush` and writes triangle vertex positions to `aux_data` — read zeros (or whatever stale entries the buffer still held from the most-recent NON-z-layered frame's bake). Rendered output: triangles at content-space origin.\n\nPRIM_RECT primitives (`fill_rect`, the node bodies) compute their own position from `bounds` directly, no aux_data dependency. They tracked viewport changes correctly, masking the bug. Glass / MSAA paths use a different upload path and also weren't affected.\n\n\nThe z-layered branch fires when `max_layer \u003e 0`, i.e. any element in the tree has `stack_layer(N)` for N≥1. Node-editor demo uses `stack_layer(1)` for the header chrome icons that sit above the canvas bg grid, so `max_layer = 1` and this branch is taken. Demos without any z\u003e0 element take the simpler full-batch path below (`else` branch at ~line 9913) which dispatches the original batch directly — aux_data is correct there.\n\n\nOne-liner, alongside the existing `.paths.clone()`:\n\n```rust\nz0_batch.aux_data = batch.aux_data.clone();\n```\n\nBoth `primitives` and `aux_data` are owned by the batch and have to follow any splice. Companion to [[gotcha-path-overlay-msaa-only-dispatch]] (same session, same web-1×-sample target, different cache miss).\n\n\nWhen constructing a temporary `PrimitiveBatch` for partial dispatch in this file, always clone `aux_data` alongside `primitives` / `paths`. The fields aren't optional: every MESH primitive in any layer needs the aux_data it indexes into.\n\nSearch-and-confirm sites: `grep -n 'PrimitiveBatch::new\\(\\)' crates/blinc_app/src/context.rs` — anywhere that builds a partial batch and then runs it through any `render_*` method that uploads aux_data.\n\n\nThree-trace pinpoint:\n\n1. **canvas closure invocation count** (motion.rs:1702) — confirmed the walker fires every frame.\n2. **canvas-kit viewport state** (lib.rs:925) — confirmed `zoom` updates live across scroll-wheel events.\n3. **emitted primitive count** — confirmed prim_count varies with zoom (background grid expands as you zoom out).\n\nOnce all three were live and dynamic, the bug had to be downstream in the GPU dispatch path. Traced through `render_tree_with_motion_opt` → no-compositor branch → z-layered split → z0_batch construction. The aux_data drop was visible by inspection once attention was on that specific line.\n\nThe non-trivial part was ruling out the upstream possibilities first (texture-pool caching, walker skipping, viewport state lag) — all of which would have been EASIER bugs but weren't this one.","files":null}]}